// The unwrapped form composes a provider output with ARBITRARY Cedar —
// things the closed `guardrails { … }` grammar cannot express:
//
//   * mixing a provider atom with a plain Cedar condition on
//     `context.input` under `&&`;
//   * using the provider's integer output inside arithmetic
//     (`.count + 1 <= 3`), not just a bare comparison.
//
// Permit Read when the request is flagged trusted AND the document has at
// most two digits (expressed as `digitCount + 1 <= 3`), where the digit
// count comes from the `Strings::DigitCount` provider.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when {
    context.input.trusted == true
    && Strings::DigitCount(context.input.document).count + 1 <= 3
};
